Z||000000||Dan Robinson||05-24-2001||04:11 AM||||My 2.5 "Iron Duke" went kablooie and I don't want to put another one of those in.  I don't have the money to put in a engine that wasn't on the options list. (I can't afford a kit to put a non option engine in) I figured it would be cheaper to put the 2.8 V6 because I may not have to alter it that much.  Any help at all would be very appreciated.  Thank You||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-24-2001||06:58 AM||||the 85+ years from what i understand are direct bolt in. i dont even think you have to change the ECM (probley wrong about that though)  you will need little things like a dog bone, engine mounts...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-24-2001||07:20 AM||||...air filter housing and ducts, engine harness, and I believe the ECM or at least the chip has to be changed. And the fuel pump. The 4-cyl fuel pump doesn't have enough pressure for the V-6.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||07:14 PM||||What about a tranny?  Shouldn't you get a Getrag if you're going with a 2.8?  If I was going to do an engine swap, I'd try to get cradle with both the 2.8 and getrag already in it.  I dont think the isuzu tranny was meant to take the 2.8, Im not sure about muncie trannys.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
